Many people think:

FAISS = an algorithm.

It isn't.

FAISS is a library developed by Meta.

Think of it like this:

NumPy
is a library.

Inside NumPy there are many algorithms.

Similarly,

FAISS
is a library that provides multiple indexing/search algorithms, including:

Flat Index (Exact Search)

IVF (Inverted File Index)

HNSW

Product Quantization (PQ)

IVF + PQ

GPU-accelerated indexes

So HNSW is an algorithm, while FAISS is a toolkit that implements algorithms like HNSW.

That distinction is another common interview question.

