HNSW vs IVF
This is a classic interview question.

IVF	HNSW
Divides vectors into clusters	Connects vectors into a graph
Searches selected clusters	Walks through neighboring vectors
Faster indexing	Slower indexing
Very memory efficient	Uses more memory
Good for huge datasets	Often gives higher recall (finds results closer to the true nearest neighbors)
Neither is "better" in every situation.

It depends on your application.

